<reading-questions xml:id="reflections-det-by-row-red">
<title>Reflect on your understanding</title>

<exercise>
	<title>Proof patterns</title>
	<p> Summarize the main idea(s) of the reasoning behind each of the statements in <xref ref="proposition-det-by-row-red-det-vs-row-ops" />. </p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
	<title>Determinant of a transpose</title>
	<p> Explain in your own words why a square matrix and its transpose always have the same determinant value. </p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
	<title>Determinants of elementary matrices</title>
	<p>
	State the determinant pattern for each of the three types of elementary matrices,
	and the reasoning for that pattern based on a particular statement from <xref ref="proposition-det-by-row-red-det-vs-row-ops" />.
	</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
	<title>Determinants of scalar multiples</title>

	<p>
	<alert>True or false:</alert>
	For every square matrix <m>A</m> and every scalar value <m>k</m>,
	it is always true that <m>\det (k A) = k \det A</m>.
	</p>

	<p>
	If the statement is true,
	explain the reasoning behind it;
	if it is false,
	state the correct relationship and explain the reasoning behind that relationship.
	</p>

</exercise>

</reading-questions>
